{
  "name": "redeeming a roster entry proves the address, and removal revokes without deleting",
  "description": "ADR-0016 §3: a roster entry is an allowlist, not a credential. Being listed is a guessable fact — anyone can guess that alex@acme.com works at Acme — so being listed is never sufficient, and the seat is created only by somebody who can read the address's inbox.\n\nTHE SILENCE COMES FIRST, because it is the property most easily lost. /auth/hirer/redeem/start answers 202 for a roster miss, for an organisation that does not exist, and for one that exists but is unverified, exactly as it does for a hit. Answering differently for any of them turns the endpoint into an oracle for who a company is hiring, which is the thing a roster must never become. Since the status cannot differ, these steps assert the ABSENCE of a message: the only observable difference between a hit and a miss is whether an inbox received anything, and for a miss it did not. ADR-0016's endpoint table says '401' here while §3 and §5 require indistinguishability; a 401 for a miss beside a 202 for a hit IS the oracle §3 forbids, so the decision list wins and the discrepancy is the Planner's to settle.\n\nTHE ORGANISATION PINS THE NAME AND THE ROLE (§2). The redeemer chooses a password and nothing else. This case sends a username and a role in the redemption body and asserts that both are ignored: a redeemer who could name themselves could take a colleague's name, or claim an owner seat and roster further people from it.\n\nTHE PROOF IS SINGLE-USE AND LIVES 24 HOURS (§7), with resend. A resend leaves exactly one live token, because the stored form is a hash and two outstanding proofs would be two ways in.\n\nREMOVAL REVOKES AND NEVER DELETES (§8, §9). The seat is stamped, its session families die, it stays listed as active:false so the author of an old round remains resolvable, and its username is never reissued.",
  "seed": ["principals"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "A ROSTER MISS. Acme is real and verified; ghost@acme.com is on nobody's roster.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/start",
        "body": {
          "org_slug": "acme",
          "email": "ghost@acme.com"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "_note": "202, and byte-identical to the hit later in this case. Nothing is minted.",
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "where": {
              "email": "ghost@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "ghost@acme.com",
          "count": 0
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "The real assertion. The status cannot tell a hit from a miss, so what must be checked is that no inbox was touched.",
        "body": null
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "An organisation that does not exist. Same answer again.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/start",
        "body": {
          "org_slug": "no-such-company",
          "email": "hopeful@nowhere.example"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "where": {
              "email": "hopeful@nowhere.example"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "hopeful@nowhere.example",
          "count": 0
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": null
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "An UNVERIFIED organisation with a real entry on a real roster. Pat owns Unknown Ltd and rosters a colleague.",
      "as": "pending_pat",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b003/roster",
        "body": {
          "email": "colleague@unknown.example",
          "username": "colleague",
          "role": "member"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "email": "colleague@unknown.example",
          "username": "colleague",
          "role": "member",
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c002",
            "username": "pat",
            "display_name": "Pat Ferreira",
            "active": true
          },
          "redeemed_at": null,
          "redeemed_by": null,
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/start",
        "body": {
          "org_slug": "unknown-ltd",
          "email": "colleague@unknown.example"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "_note": "Still 202. Three distinct causes — no entry, no organisation, no verification — and one answer.",
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "where": {
              "email": "colleague@unknown.example"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "colleague@unknown.example",
          "count": 0
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": null
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Now the hit. Hank rosters Rita as a MEMBER of Acme.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/roster",
        "body": {
          "email": "rita@acme.com",
          "username": "rita",
          "role": "member"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "rita_entry": "$.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "email": "rita@acme.com",
          "username": "rita",
          "role": "member",
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "redeemed_at": null,
          "redeemed_by": null,
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/start",
        "body": {
          "org_slug": "acme",
          "email": "rita@acme.com"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "_note": "202 and an empty body, indistinguishable from the three misses above. What differs is the row, and the message.",
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com",
              "purpose": "roster_redemption"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "consumed_at": null
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The proof reaches the INBOX and nowhere else. It is minted once, stored as a hash, and returned by no endpoint — so reading the message is the only way anyone, including this suite, can obtain it.",
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "rita@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "count": 1
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "rita_proof": "$.token"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "A message carrying no token is a dead end for its recipient: they are told to confirm an address and given nothing to confirm it with. That is what this step fails on.",
        "body": {
          "to": "rita@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "html": "<string>",
          "token": "<token>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A redemption that tries to name ITSELF. The body asks for the username 'impostor' and an OWNER seat, and is refused outright.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "{{rita_proof}}",
          "display_name": "Rita Sandoval",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery",
          "username": "impostor",
          "role": "owner"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 400,
        "_note": "400, not a 201 that quietly overrules the extras. Every body in this codebase is decoded with DisallowUnknownFields, and that convention lands exactly right here: a redeemer cannot even ASK for a name or a role, rather than asking and being silently overruled. Refusing is the stronger reading of ADR-0016 §2 — and it also tells an honest client with a stale field that its request did nothing, instead of letting it believe it chose the seat it was given.",
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_registration"
        },
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "_note": "THE PROOF IS NOT SPENT. Decoding fails before any service is called, so a malformed request cannot burn a single-use token — which would otherwise let anyone holding a leaked link, or a client with one stale field, lock the rightful holder out of the seat entirely.",
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "consumed_at": null
            }
          },
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 0
          },
          "organization_hirer_roster": {
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "redeemed_at": null
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The same proof, well formed. The username and the role are read from the ENTRY and appear nowhere in the request — which is what makes them the organisation's choice rather than the redeemer's (ADR-0016 §2).",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "{{rita_proof}}",
          "display_name": "Rita Sandoval",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "rita_token": "$.access_token",
        "rita_id": "$.hirer.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "201 with a token pair, unlike registration, which returns no credential. Registration queues a review; a redeemed entry was already approved by the organisation that wrote it, so there is nothing left to wait for. verified is true because ACME is verified — capability is a property of the organisation (ADR-0002).",
        "body": {
          "hirer": {
            "id": "<uuid>",
            "display_name": "Rita Sandoval",
            "email": "rita@acme.com",
            "principal_type": "hirer",
            "verified": true,
            "organization": {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001",
              "name": "Acme Corp",
              "verified": true,
              "payment_verified": true
            }
          },
          "access_token": "<token>",
          "refresh_token": "<token>",
          "expires_in": 900
        },
        "db": {
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "_note": "The seat carries the ENTRY's username, never the request body's.",
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com",
              "username": "rita"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "disabled_at": null,
              "auth_provider": "email"
            }
          },
          "organization_hirer_roster": {
            "_note": "Stamped, not deleted. The entry is the record of why the seat exists, and removing it is what revokes access later.",
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "none_match": {
              "redeemed_at": null
            }
          },
          "email_verifications": {
            "where": {
              "email": "rita@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "none_match": {
              "consumed_at": null
            }
          },
          "organization_members": {
            "where": {
              "organization_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001",
              "role": "member"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "'impostor' was never created, and the seat is a member. Any hirer in the organisation may read the seats — every seat already sees every round, so naming their holders exposes no row that was not already visible (§9).",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/seats"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Live seats first, then revoked, each group oldest first. Rita is the newest live seat.",
        "body": {
          "seats": [
            {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
              "username": "hank",
              "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
              "email": "hank@acme.com",
              "role": "owner",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c004",
              "username": "dave_h",
              "display_name": "Dave Whitfield",
              "email": "dave.hiring@example.com",
              "role": "member",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "username": "rita",
              "display_name": "Rita Sandoval",
              "email": "rita@acme.com",
              "role": "member",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "db": {
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "where": {
              "username": "impostor"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Rita reads the same list, on her own token.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/seats",
        "headers": {
          "Authorization": "Bearer {{rita_token}}"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "seats": [
            {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
              "username": "hank",
              "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
              "email": "hank@acme.com",
              "role": "owner",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c004",
              "username": "dave_h",
              "display_name": "Dave Whitfield",
              "email": "dave.hiring@example.com",
              "role": "member",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "username": "rita",
              "display_name": "Rita Sandoval",
              "email": "rita@acme.com",
              "role": "member",
              "active": true,
              "disabled_at": null
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "...but the ROSTER is owners only, and the entry gave her a member seat. Asking for 'owner' in the redemption body bought nothing.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/roster",
        "headers": {
          "Authorization": "Bearer {{rita_token}}"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "not_an_org_member"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The proof is single-use. A mailbox read a second time buys nothing.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "{{rita_proof}}",
          "display_name": "Someone Else",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 410,
        "_note": "410 Gone rather than 401: the holder of a spent link is entitled to know which happened, because the remedy differs — sign in, rather than ask for another link. A bare 401 would send someone who already has an account round the loop again.",
        "body": {
          "error": "verification_already_used"
        },
        "db": {
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "where": {
              "display_name": "Someone Else"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A token nobody ever issued is 401 and says no more, so live proofs cannot be probed for.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "not-a-real-verification-token",
          "display_name": "Nobody",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 401,
        "body": {
          "error": "email_verification_required"
        },
        "db": {
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "where": {
              "display_name": "Nobody"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Resend, on a second address so the rotation can be watched from a clean inbox. This entry pins OWNER.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/orgs/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/roster",
        "body": {
          "email": "mo@acme.com",
          "username": "mo",
          "role": "owner"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "mo_entry": "$.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "email": "mo@acme.com",
          "username": "mo",
          "role": "owner",
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "redeemed_at": null,
          "redeemed_by": null,
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/start",
        "body": {
          "org_slug": "acme",
          "email": "mo@acme.com"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "body": null
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "mo@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "count": 1
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "mo_first_proof": "$.token"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "to": "mo@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "html": "<string>",
          "token": "<token>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "202 and silent, exactly like start: an address with no proof outstanding must not be distinguishable from one with a link in flight.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/verify/resend",
        "body": {
          "email": "mo@acme.com"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "email_verifications": {
            "_note": "Two rows, and exactly one of them live. The stored form is a hash, so the original plaintext is gone and a resend cannot repeat it — it rotates. Two outstanding proofs would be two ways in, with the first still valid after the second was issued.",
            "where": {
              "email": "mo@acme.com"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "system",
      "request": {
        "method": "READ_EMAIL",
        "path": "/",
        "body": {
          "to": "mo@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "count": 2
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "mo_second_proof": "$.token"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "to": "mo@acme.com",
          "subject": "Confirm your email address",
          "html": "<string>",
          "token": "<token>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The superseded link is dead.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "{{mo_first_proof}}",
          "display_name": "Mo Adeyemi",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 410,
        "body": {
          "error": "verification_already_used"
        },
        "db": {
          "hirer_accounts": {
            "where": {
              "username": "mo"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "The newest one works, and carries the OWNER role the entry pinned.",
      "as": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/auth/hirer/redeem/complete",
        "body": {
          "token": "{{mo_second_proof}}",
          "display_name": "Mo Adeyemi",
          "password": "correct-horse-battery"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "hirer": {
            "id": "<uuid>",
            "display_name": "Mo Adeyemi",
            "email": "mo@acme.com",
            "principal_type": "hirer",
            "verified": true,
            "organization": {
              "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001",
